# repro.log — vite-cve-2025-31125 (CVE-2025-30208 -> CVE-2025-31125)
# generated: 2026-07-11
# Vite dev-server /@fs/ arbitrary-file-read; server.fs allow/deny bypass via query-suffix tricks.
# per-run canary token planted at /canary.txt (OUTSIDE Vite project root /app) via compose
# entrypoint from $PCB_FLAG. Only reachable through the /@fs/ file-read bypass.

## Recipe bring-up (Dockerfile per version; ARG VITE_VERSION -> npm i vite@<ver>; no vendored source)
  PCB_FLAG=<token> docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 up -d
  # entrypoint: writes $PCB_FLAG -> /canary.txt, then `npx vite --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173`
  # oracle.py --run-gate does the whole up -> gate -> down cycle automatically (v0+v1)

## Vectors (curl --path-as-is; the multiple `?` are all part of the query string)
  original (CVE-2025-30208, trailing-sep) : /@fs/canary.txt?import&raw??
  bypass   (CVE-2025-31125, raw?import)   : /@fs/canary.txt?raw?import
  baseline (no trick)                     : /@fs/canary.txt

## Mechanism (from patch.diff, packages/vite/src/node/server/middlewares/transform.ts)
  V1 (5.4.15) CVE-2025-30208 fix strips trailing `[?&]+$` then runs rawRE/urlRE + ensureServingAccess,
     so `?raw??` is now normalized -> detected -> access-checked -> BLOCKED.
  BUT V1's rawRE/urlRE only matched `raw` at query-end or before `&`, so `?raw?import` did NOT match
     -> the serving-access guard was SKIPPED, while the raw loader still read the file => residual.
  V2 (5.4.16) CVE-2025-31125 fix replaces the guard regexes with /[?&]raw\b/ (+ adds inlineRE),
     so `?raw?import` now matches -> BLOCKED.

